From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:02:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Leave the screen saver when the system resumes from suspend

- A screen saver started before a suspend stayed after the resume: the key
  that wakes the system never reaches ES. The main loop now compares
  CLOCK_BOOTTIME with CLOCK_MONOTONIC (SDL's ticks do not count the time
  asleep): after a resume the screen saver stops and the idle times start
  over, as on a key, and the next frame is drawn whatever it holds.
---
 es-app/src/main.cpp    |  2 ++
 es-core/src/Window.cpp | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 es-core/src/Window.h   |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/es-app/src/main.cpp b/es-app/src/main.cpp
index 2e58cf61..97f2d08a 100644
--- a/es-app/src/main.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/main.cpp
@@ -728,6 +728,8 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
 		  //	ps_time = SDL_GetTicks();
 		}
 
+		window.checkSystemResume();
+
 		if (window.isSleeping())
 		{
 			lastTime = SDL_GetTicks();
diff --git a/es-core/src/Window.cpp b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
index f9d1a429..38c9d749 100644
--- a/es-core/src/Window.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <SDL_events.h>
 #include "ThemeData.h"
 #include <mutex>
